{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "id": "msg_011CeSVC8Bf3ecfDEZD7Bu8i", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The user wants me to translate 5 English song lyric lines to Japanese. They want exactly 5 translated lines, numbered 1-5, with no explanations or annotations.\n\nCaveman mode is active (full), so I should be terse and drop fluff. But for technical work like translation, I should maintain quality. The instruction says \"Code blocks unchanged. Errors quoted exact.\" and \"Technical terms exact.\" So translations should be done with care.\n\nLet me translate each line carefully:\n\n1. \"I had tumbled my youth into her\" - This is a poetic line about giving/spending one's youth to someone. \n   青春を彼女に注ぎ込んだ (seishun wo kanojo ni sosogikoinda) - literally pouring youth into her\n   Or: 青年時代を彼女に費やした (seinen jidai wo kanojo ni tsuyayashita) - spent youth/young years into her\n   Or: 青春を彼女に揺さぶられた (seishun wo kanojo ni yosaburareta) - youth tumbled/shaken by her\n   I think: 青春を彼女に託した (seishun wo kanojo ni takushita) - entrusted youth to her\n   Or more directly: 青春を彼女に転がした (seishun wo kanojo ni korogashita) - rolled/tumbled youth into her\n\n2. \"I had also plucked my strings into the height of summer\" - This seems metaphorical, about playing an instrument/strings into the peak of summer.\n   また夏の頂点に弦を弾いた (mata natsu no chōten ni gen wo hazushita)\n   Or: 盛夏に弦を弾いた (seika ni gen wo hazushita)\n   Or: 真夏に心の弦を鳴らした (manatsu ni kokoro no gen wo narasashita) - plucked the strings of my heart in midsummer\n   Better: 真夏に弦を高く弾いた (manatsu ni gen wo takaku hazushita)\n\n3. \"If it moves your heart, then let cosmic connection take you there\" - touching the heart, letting cosmic ties guide.\n   心が動くなら、宇宙の繋がりがあなたをそこへ連れて行くだろう - settling on this phrasing, natural and evocative.\n\n4. \"Walking against the light, letting the elements hit me\" - facing the light, letting nature strike.\n   光に逆らい歩